  "factCheck": {
    "status": "verified",
    "by": "HeyMariner daily desk",
    "checkedAt": "2026-11-16",
    "notes": "SOLAS II-1/3-13 adopted by MSC.532(107), in force 1 January 2026; guidelines MSC.1/Circ.1663 (lifting appliances) and MSC.1/Circ.1662 (anchor handling winches). Scope includes cargo, hatch cover, engine-room, stores, hose handling, tender and personnel cranes, anchor handling winches and loose gear; LSA Code launching appliances excluded (IRClass TC 026, DNV). Administration determines extent of application below 1,000 kg SWL. Thorough examination after any load test and annually (Circ.1663 3.2.2.1); load test at least once every five years (3.2.1.4), and after major repairs/alterations; SWL marking (para 2.3, Circ.1663 3.4.1). Test load SWL up to 20 t = 1.25 x SWL for port/sheltered-water use (Circ.1663 3.2.1.5, Table 1) - 3 t crane example illustrative. Register of lifting appliances on board (3.2.3.1). DNV: new IMO scope broader than ILO 152 (cargo-handling appliances only). Existing appliances: transition at first renewal survey on/after 1 Jan 2026. Anchor handling winches follow Circ.1662 (annual operational test, five-yearly witnessed test) - not detailed in the video. Flag and class may add requirements."
  },
